  "narrative": "The RaMP enrichment analysis of the ten metabolites returned one overwhelmingly significant pathway: **Eicosanoid synthesis** (Wikipathways WP167, FDR = 0.0, fold enrichment = 1,000.76). Five of the input compounds map to this pathway — arachidonic acid (C00219), leukotriene A4 (C00909), 15-HETE (C04742), 5-HETE (C04805), and 15-deoxy-Δ12,14-PGJ2 (C14717). Membership of arachidonic acid and leukotriene A4 within the Arachidonic Acid Metabolism pathway was independently confirmed via `query_pathway_membership`, with plausibility scores of 1.0 for all five co-observed metabolites. A directed BFS query through the KEGG reaction graph confirmed that **arachidonic acid is metabolically upstream of leukotriene A4**, proceeding via the prostaglandin endoperoxide intermediate (C05356) in two enzymatic steps.\n\n**Affected pathway and drivers.** The primary affected pathway is eicosanoid biosynthesis centred on arachidonic acid metabolism. Arachidonic acid serves as the obligate precursor; its oxidation via the 5-lipoxygenase pathway yields 5-HETE and leukotriene A4, while the 15-lipoxygenase branch produces 15-HETE. The cyclopentenone prostaglandin 15-deoxy-Δ12,14-PGJ2 arises from the cyclooxygenase cascade. Leukotriene A4 is the direct downstream product of arachidonic acid in the leukotriene axis, making it a key driver of the observed dysregulation. The simultaneous elevation of 5-HETE and 15-HETE alongside leukotriene A4 suggests broad activation of lipoxygenase pathways.\n\n**Biological significance.** Eicosanoids are potent lipid mediators governing inflammation, vasomotor tone, and immune cell chemotaxis. Elevated leukotriene A4 and its product 5-HETE point to active neutrophil recruitment and airway inflammation. 15-HETE and 15-deoxy-PGJ2 are associated with resolution-phase inflammation and PPAR-γ activation, respectively, suggesting a complex interplay between pro-inflammatory and anti-inflammatory programs. The presence of histamine indicates mast cell activation, which synergises with leukotrienes to amplify allergic-type responses.\n\n**Secondary annotation.** The selenium micronutrient network also reached FDR = 0.0, enriched for hypochlorite, copper, arachidonic acid, and the lipoxygenase products, plausibly reflecting antioxidant and redox-dependent regulation of eicosanoid metabolism. In summary, the treatment group shows strong activation of the arachidonic acid–eicosanoid axis with verified upstream-to-downstream connectivity from arachidonic acid through prostaglandin intermediates to leukotriene A4 and parallel 5-/15-HETE production, consistent with an inflammatory stimulus that engages both the lipoxygenase and cyclooxygenase arms of the pathway.",
